Upstream-bound: no
Subject: [PORT_HOST] menus: instant exit from the field menu's screens to the field

Owner feedback (preview p57, FEEDBACK-p57-1): "when I leave the items screen or
the map (the pause menu in general) the transition animation plays. I don't want
that animation." Leaving the field menu's screens for the walking field is the
field menu in the status mode (STSTATUS) closing with Triangle: its three
panels fold (about 15 frames, kept), then updateFieldMenu state 2 plays the
block dissolve (stepFieldMenuFade / drawFieldMenuFade: six 64-pixel block
sprites through darker CLUT rows, two vsyncs a row, 96 frames at 60 Hz) and
state 2's substate 6 requests GAME.fieldMode.

With the key menu_instant_exit on (Options > Menus > Instant menu exit, default
on; DW3_MENU_INSTANT_EXIT=0 forces it off for a run), state 2 in the status mode
steps stepFieldMenuFade's state machine to its end in the same update and draws
nothing. Each skipped frame calls dw3_port_menu_exit_frame (port/menu_exit),
which adds what a frame adds in the original loop: the vsync, frame and play
time counters, the play time clock (updatePlayTime) and one RANDOM.next(). The
mode request, GAME.fieldMode, the position and the argument are exactly the
original's, reached with the clocks and the RNG where the animation would have
left them. Skipped on purpose: the pad, the file cache, the sound loader and the
music ticks of those frames, which only serve the screen being left.

Only the exit to the field changes. Going into a screen from the field (state 2
outside the status mode), the other modes' exits and the battle transition are
the original's. One log line per exit: `dw3-menu: exit to field instant (skipped
N transition frames, from <screen>)`, or `... with the original transition
(instant exit off, from <screen>)` with the key off.

--- a/src/engine/menu/field_menu.c
+++ b/src/engine/menu/field_menu.c
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
 #include "port_confirm.h"
 #include "port_field_options.h"
 #include "port_turbo.h"
+#include "port_menu_exit.h"
 /* P6.27: language of the Return to title row (the EU disc's LANGUAGE; the US
    disc is English). */
 #if VERSION_EU
@@ -627,6 +628,34 @@
         }
         break;
     case 2:
+#if PORT_HOST
+        /* Instant menu exit (docs/P6.34_MENU_FLOW.md section 16): leaving the
+           status mode for the field, the fade's frames are run in one go (each
+           with the counters, the play time and the RNG step a frame adds) and
+           nothing of it is drawn. Going into a screen from the field keeps the
+           dissolve. */
+        if (GAME.funcs.getMode() == MODE_STATUS && task->substate < 7) {
+            if (dw3_port_menu_instant_exit_enabled()) {
+                s32 skipped = 0;
+
+                /* the fade lasts under 100 frames; the bound only keeps a stuck
+                   clock from hanging the loop (the next frame goes on) */
+                while (skipped < 600) {
+                    stepFieldMenuFade(task);
+                    if (task->substate >= 7) {
+                        dw3_port_menu_exit_report(1, skipped, FIELD_MENU_CHOICE.option, FIELD_MENU_CHOICE.extra);
+                        break;
+                    }
+                    dw3_port_menu_exit_frame();
+                    skipped++;
+                }
+                break;
+            }
+            if (task->substate == 6) {
+                dw3_port_menu_exit_report(0, 0, FIELD_MENU_CHOICE.option, FIELD_MENU_CHOICE.extra);
+            }
+        }
+#endif
         stepFieldMenuFade(task);
         drawFieldMenuFade(task);
         break;
